\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Jesus, Thy blood and righteousness
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj My beauty are, my glorious dress:
\par Midst flaming worlds, in these arrayed,
\par With joy shall I lift up my head.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  Bold shall I stand in Thy great day;
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj For who ought to my charge shall give
\par Fully absolved through these I am,
\par From sin and fear, from guilt and shame.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. The holy, meek, unspotted Lamb,
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0 Who from the Father's bosom came,
\par Who died for me, ev'n  to atone,
\par Now for my Lord and God I owe.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  Lord, I believe Thy precious blood,
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0   Which at the mercy-seat of God
\par   For ever doth for sinners plead,
\par  For me, even  my soul, was shed.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.  When from the dust of death I rise
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0  To claim my mansion in the skies
\par   Ev'n then this shall be all my plea
\par   Jesus hath lived, hath died for me:
\par \pard\li360\sl200\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  Jesus, be endless praise to Thee,
\par \pard\li360\sl200\slmult0 Whose boundless mercy hath for me,
\par For me and all Thy hands have made,
\par An everlasting ransom paid.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li360\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par   7.  Lord, I believe, were sinners more
\par \pard\li360\sl200\slmult0 Than sands upon the ocean shore,
\par Thou hast for all a ransom paid,
\par For all a full atonement made.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8.  Ah! Give to all Thy servants, Lord,
\par \pard\li360\sl200\slmult0\qj  With pow'r to speak Thy gracious word,
\par That all who to Thy wounds will flee,
\par May find eternal life in Thee.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li360\sl200\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9.  Thou God of pow'r, Thou God of  Love,
\par \pard\li360\sl200\slmult0\qj Let the whole world Thy mercy prove!
\par Now let Thy word o'er all prevail;
\par Now take the spoils of death and hell.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

